diff --git a/forth/cross.4 b/forth/cross.4
index 9a4fc04..af4bc1f 100644
--- a/forth/cross.4
+++ b/forth/cross.4
@@ -204,9 +204,8 @@ VARIABLE NAMELEN
   THEN
   THERE TLINK !
   THERE THIS-THREAD @ CELLS TTHREADS + !
-  THERE C@-T 128 OR THERE C!-T
   NAMELEN @ 1+ ALLOT-T ALIGN-T ;
-      \ Set bit 7 of count byte as a marker.
+      \ (bit 7 of the count byte no longer a marker - Iteration 244)
 
 \ : "HEADER CREATE ALIGN-T ;  \ Alternative for "HEADER in case the target system
                       \ is just an application without headers.
@@ -359,6 +358,19 @@ FORTH DEFINITIONS
   PREVIOUS
 ;
 
+\ The IMMEDIATE bit of the target word whose code is t-xt (Iteration 244):
+\ its header is found along the thread its name hashes to (T-THREAD, set by
+\ POSTPONE) - there is no marker byte to scan back for. 0 when not found.
+VARIABLE T-XT
+VARIABLE T-THREAD
+: TNAME> ( t-nfa --- t-xt )  DUP C@-T 31 AND 1+ + ALIGNED-T ;
+: T-IMMEDIATE? ( t-xt --- flag )
+  T-XT !  T-THREAD @ CELLS TTHREADS + @
+  BEGIN DUP WHILE
+    DUP TNAME> T-XT @ = IF C@-T 64 AND EXIT THEN
+    TARGET-CELL-BYTES @ - DUP @-T DUP IF + ELSE SWAP DROP THEN
+  REPEAT ;
+
 : >BODY-T ( t-addr1 --- t-addr2 ) \ Convert executing token to param address.
   \ NOTE: this is target-address arithmetic and must use CELLS-T, not the
   \ host's CELLS. It only worked before because the host (RelF, 4-byte
@@ -437,7 +449,14 @@ FORWARD (POSTPONE)
 \ delimiters, so an empty string took the rest of the line (kernel.4's ABORT).
 : ." [ TRANSIENT ] (.") [ FORTH ] 34 PARSE DUP 1+ >R
       THERE PLACE-T R> ALLOT-T ALIGN-T ;
-: POSTPONE [ TRANSIENT ] (POSTPONE) [ FORTH ] T' THERE - ,-T ;
+\ Iteration 244: a target POSTPONE decides immediacy here, from the target
+\ header's IMMEDIATE bit - an immediate word compiled as a call (it runs when
+\ the definition runs), any other through (POSTPONE), which compiles it. The
+\ kernel's (POSTPONE) no longer asks >NAME at run time (a scan back for a
+\ marked byte, broken by UTF-8 names; bit 7 marks nothing now).
+: POSTPONE >IN @ BL WORD COUNT THASH T-THREAD ! >IN !
+  T' DUP T-IMMEDIATE? IF THERE - CELLBYTES-TOKEN - ,-T
+  ELSE [ TRANSIENT ] (POSTPONE) [ FORTH ] THERE - ,-T THEN ;
 : ABORT" [ TRANSIENT ] (ABORT") [ FORTH ] 34 PARSE DUP 1+ >R
       THERE PLACE-T R> ALLOT-T ALIGN-T ;
 
diff --git a/forth/cv8b.4 b/forth/cv8b.4
index 109187a..d297210 100644
--- a/forth/cv8b.4
+++ b/forth/cv8b.4
@@ -89,7 +89,22 @@ VARIABLE HDR-LEN
   HERE DUP HDR-LEN @ + HERE C@ 1+ CMOVE>
   HDR-HEAD @ IF HERE HDR-LEN @ + HDR-HEAD @ - ELSE 0 THEN HDR-LEN @ LINK,
   HERE LAST !
-  HERE C@ 1+ HERE C@ 128 + HERE C! ALLOT ;
+  HERE C@ 1+ ALLOT ;      \ bit 7 no longer marks the count byte (Iteration 244)
+
+: >NAME8 ( xt --- nfa | 0 )
+\ The kernel's >NAME on byte headers (Iteration 244): the same walk, with
+\ NEXT-NFA8 and NAME>8; the converter puts this body into >NAME.
+  >NAME-XT !
+  #ORDER @ BEGIN DUP WHILE 1-
+    DUP CELLS CONTEXT + @  DUP @
+    BEGIN DUP WHILE
+      2DUP CELLS + @
+      BEGIN DUP WHILE
+        DUP NAME>8 >NAME-XT @ = IF >R 2DROP DROP R> EXIT THEN
+        NEXT-NFA8
+      REPEAT DROP 1-
+    REPEAT 2DROP
+  REPEAT DROP 0 ;
 
 \ ---- the search -----------------------------------------------------
 : NAME=? ( a1 a2 u --- flag )
